95,996],{"class":82,"line":83},[80,997,998],{"class":208},"\u002F\u002F Schedule a microtask — runs after current task, before any macrotask\n",[80,1000,1001,1003,1005,1007],{"class":82,"line":104},[80,1002,46],{"class":90},[80,1004,116],{"class":86},[80,1006,120],{"class":119},[80,1008,535],{"class":86},[80,1010,1011,1013,1015,1017,1020],{"class":82,"line":111},[80,1012,559],{"class":86},[80,1014,91],{"class":90},[80,1016,94],{"class":86},[80,1018,1019],{"class":97},"'runs as microtask'",[80,1021,101],{"class":86},[80,1023,1024],{"class":82,"line":142},[80,1025,569],{"class":86},[80,1027,1028],{"class":82,"line":147},[80,1029,108],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":107},[80,1031,1032],{"class":82,"line":181},[80,1033,1034],{"class":208},"\u002F\u002F vs setTimeout (macrotask)\n",[80,1036,1037,1039,1041,1043],{"class":82,"line":186},[80,1038,57],{"class":90},[80,1040,116],{"class":86},[80,1042,120],{"class":119},[80,1044,535],{"class":86},[80,1046,1047,1049,1051,1053,1056],{"class":82,"line":200},[80,1048,559],{"class":86},[80,1050,91],{"class":90},[80,1052,94],{"class":86},[80,1054,1055],{"class":97},"'runs as macrotask'",[80,1057,101],{"class":86},[80,1059,1060,1063,1065],{"class":82,"line":205},[80,1061,1062],{"class":86},"}, ",[80,1064,137],{"class":136},[80,1066,101],{"class":86},[80,1068,1069],{"class":82,"line":212},[80,1070,108],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":107},[80,1072,1073],{"class":82,"line":351},[80,1074,1075],{"class":208},"\u002F\u002F queueMicrotask runs first\n",[19,1077,218],{},[14,1079,1081],{"id":1080},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[19,1083,1084,1087,1088,153],{},[29,1085,1086],{},"Microtasks run between macrotasks"," — If you queue a microtask from a macrotask, it runs before the next macrotask. Useful for batching DOM updates: ",[40,1089,1090],{},"queueMicrotask(() => render())",[19,1092,1093,1096,1097,1100],{},[29,1094,1095],{},"setTimeout(fn, 0) is not \"immediate\""," — It's \"after all microtasks.\" There's always a delay. Use ",[40,1098,1099],{},"Promise.resolve().then()"," if you need to defer without delay.",[19,1102,1103,1106,1107,1110,1111,1114],{},[29,1104,1105],{},"Inspect microtask vs macrotask timing"," — Put ",[40,1108,1109],{},"console.time","\u002F",[40,1112,1113],{},"console.timeEnd"," around code to see actual delays. Helps diagnose event loop issues.",[19,1116,1117,38,1120,1123,1124,1127,1128,1131],{},[29,1118,1119],{},"Promises in loops serialize",[40,1121,1122],{},"promises.map(p => p.then(...))"," is fine, but ",[40,1125,1126],{},"promises.forEach(p => await p)"," is slow (sequential). Use ",[40,1129,1130],{},"Promise.all()"," for parallelism.",[14,1133,1135],{"id":1134},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[19,1137,1138,38,1141,1144],{},[29,1139,1140],{},"setTimeout with small delays don't work",[40,1142,1143],{},"setTimeout(fn, 0)"," is clamped to 4ms minimum in browsers (1ms in some). Actual delay can be much longer if event loop is busy.",[19,1146,1147,1150,1151,153],{},[29,1148,1149],{},"Blocking the event loop hangs the browser"," — Long loops, crypto operations, or heavy parsing freeze the UI. Move work to Web Workers or break into chunks with ",[40,1152,57],{},[19,1154,1155,1158],{},[29,1156,1157],{},"Callbacks aren't truly concurrent"," — They're interleaved on a single thread. If callback A takes 10ms, callback B waits. This isn't \"parallel\" like threads; it's \"cooperative concurrency.\"",[19,1160,1161,1164,1165,1167,1168,1170],{},[29,1162,1163],{},"Promise and setTimeout interleaving is confusing"," — Microtasks queue differently than macrotasks. ",[40,1166,57],{}," -> run one -> check microtasks -> ",[40,1169,57],{}," -> ... . Hard to reason about without drawing diagrams.",[19,1172,1173,1176],{},[29,1174,1175],{},"Forgotten callbacks leak memory"," — If a callback captures huge data and is never called, the data is kept alive. Subscriptions without unsubscribe are a common leak source.",[19,1178,1179,38,1182,1185,1186,1189],{},[29,1180,1181],{},"Mixing Promise and callback styles is error-prone",[40,1183,1184],{},"asyncFn().then().catch()"," and ",[40,1187,1188],{},".catch((err) => callback(err))"," style can cause double-handling or missed errors. Use one style consistently.",[14,1191,1193],{"id":1192},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[19,1195,1196],{},"What's the output order?",[68,1198,1199],{"language":70},[72,1200,1202],{"className":74,"code":1201,"language":70,"meta":76,"style":76},"console.log('1')\n\nsetTimeout(() => console.log('2'), 0)\n\nPromise.resolve()\n  .then(() => {\n    console.log('3')\n    return new Promise(resolve => {\n      resolve()\n      console.log('4')\n    })\n  })\n  .then(() => console.log('5'))\n\nqueueMicrotask(() => console.log('6'))\n\nconsole.log('7')\n",[40,1203,1204,1217,1221,1244,1248,1258,1270,1284,1303,1310,1324,1328,1332,1353,1357,1376,1380],{"__ignoreMap":76},[80,1205,1206,1208,1210,1212,1215],{"class":82,"line":83},[80,1207,87],{"class":86},[80,1209,91],{"class":90},[80,1211,94],{"class":86},[80,1213,1214],{"class":97},"'1'",[80,1216,101],{"class":86},[80,1218,1219],{"class":82,"line":104},[80,1220,108],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":107},[80,1222,1223,1225,1227,1229,1231,1233,1235,1238,1240,1242],{"class":82,"line":111},[80,1224,57],{"class":90},[80,1226,116],{"class":86},[80,1228,120],{"class":119},[80,1230,123],{"class":86},[80,1232,91],{"class":90},[80,1234,94],{"class":86},[80,1236,1237],{"class":97},"'2'",[80,1239,133],{"class":86},[80,1241,137],{"class":136},[80,1243,101],{"class":86},[80,1245,1246],{"class":82,"line":142},[80,1247,108],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":107},[80,1249,1250,1252,1254,1256],{"class":82,"line":147},[80,1251,150],{"class":136},[80,1253,153],{"class":86},[80,1255,156],{"class":90},[80,1257,284],{"class":86},[80,1259,1260,1262,1264,1266,1268],{"class":82,"line":181},[80,1261,289],{"class":86},[80,1263,162],{"class":90},[80,1265,116],{"class":86},[80,1267,120],{"class":119},[80,1269,535],{"class":86},[80,1271,1272,1275,1277,1279,1282],{"class":82,"line":186},[80,1273,1274],{"class":86},"    console.",[80,1276,91],{"class":90},[80,1278,94],{"class":86},[80,1280,1281],{"class":97},"'3'",[80,1283,101],{"class":86},[80,1285,1286,1289,1292,1295,1297,1299,1301],{"class":82,"line":200},[80,1287,1288],{"class":119},"    return",[80,1290,1291],{"class":119}," new",[80,1293,1294],{"class":136}," Promise",[80,1296,94],{"class":86},[80,1298,156],{"class":415},[80,1300,447],{"class":119},[80,1302,535],{"class":86},[80,1304,1305,1308],{"class":82,"line":205},[80,1306,1307],{"class":90},"      resolve",[80,1309,284],{"class":86},[80,1311,1312,1315,1317,1319,1322],{"class":82,"line":212},[80,1313,1314],{"class":86},"      console.",[80,1316,91],{"class":90},[80,1318,94],{"class":86},[80,1320,1321],{"class":97},"'4'",[80,1323,101],{"class":86},[80,1325,1326],{"class":82,"line":351},[80,1327,753],{"class":86},[80,1329,1330],{"class":82,"line":357},[80,1331,758],{"class":86},[80,1333,1334,1336,1338,1340,1342,1344,1346,1348,1351],{"class":82,"line":363},[80,1335,289],{"class":86},[80,1337,162],{"class":90},[80,1339,116],{"class":86},[80,1341,120],{"class":119},[80,1343,123],{"class":86},[80,1345,91],{"class":90},[80,1347,94],{"class":86},[80,1349,1350],{"class":97},"'5'",[80,1352,178],{"class":86},[80,1354,1355],{"class":82,"line":369},[80,1356,108],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":107},[80,1358,1359,1361,1363,1365,1367,1369,1371,1374],{"class":82,"line":375},[80,1360,46],{"class":90},[80,1362,116],{"class":86},[80,1364,120],{"class":119},[80,1366,123],{"class":86},[80,1368,91],{"class":90},[80,1370,94],{"class":86},[80,1372,1373],{"class":97},"'6'",[80,1375,178],{"class":86},[80,1377,1378],{"class":82,"line":381},[80,1379,108],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":107},[80,1381,1382,1384,1386,1388,1391],{"class":82,"line":958},[80,1383,87],{"class":86},[80,1385,91],{"class":90},[80,1387,94],{"class":86},[80,1389,1390],{"class":97},"'7'",[80,1392,101],{"class":86},[1394,1395,1396,1400,1407,1460],"details",{},[1397,1398,1399],"summary",{},"Answer",[19,1401,1402,1403,1406],{},"Logs: ",[40,1404,1405],{},"1 7 3 4 6 5 2",". Here's why:",[1408,1409,1410,1419,1435,1443,1452],"ul",{},[26,1411,1412,43,1415,1418],{},[40,1413,1414],{},"1",[40,1416,1417],{},"7"," — synchronous code runs first",[26,1420,1421,43,1424,1427,1428,1431,1432,1434],{},[40,1422,1423],{},"3",[40,1425,1426],{},"4"," — first promise ",[40,1429,1430],{},".then()"," runs (microtask), ",[40,1433,1426],{}," logs before resolve returns",[26,1436,1437,38,1440,1442],{},[40,1438,1439],{},"6",[40,1441,46],{}," is another microtask",[26,1444,1445,1448,1449,1451],{},[40,1446,1447],{},"5"," — second ",[40,1450,1430],{}," runs (chained microtask)",[26,1453,1454,38,1457,1459],{},[40,1455,1456],{},"2",[40,1458,57],{}," is a macrotask (runs last)",[19,1461,1462,1465,1466,1468],{},[29,1463,1464],{},"The lesson",": Microtasks run before macrotasks, even if queued later. Promise construction runs synchronously; the ",[40,1467,1430],{}," is microtask.",[14,1470,1472],{"id":1471},"key-takeaways","Key Takeaways",[1408,1474,1475,1478,1488,1491,1494],{},[26,1476,1477],{},"JS is single-threaded — async operations go to the event loop, not new threads.",[26,1479,1480,1483,1484,1487],{},[29,1481,1482],{},"Microtasks"," (Promises) run before ",[29,1485,1486],{},"macrotasks"," (setTimeout) — always.",[26,1489,1490],{},"The call stack must be empty before the event loop processes the task queue.",[26,1492,1493],{},"Callback hell is solved by Promises and async\u002Fawait — use them instead.",[26,1495,1496],{},"Error-first callback convention is standard in Node.js APIs.",[1498,1499,1500],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}h